BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Campfire Storytime\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260731T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260731T203000
UID:e65be4b9d5ef11bc05f3b134279faf81@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join the nature center mascots\, Olive the Owl and Doug the De
 er\, and a park naturalist for a story reading. We will read Mossy &nbsp\;
 by Jan Brett or another title and enjoy a small campfire at the edge of th
 e woods. Meet at the fire ring behind the Friends&#39\; Shelterhouse near 
 the Nature Center. Come early to enjoy the fire if you like! We will take 
 suggestions on kid friendly books about nature! Feel free to suggest a fav
 orite of yours to the naturalist! Owl Moon \, The Lorax \, Mossy \, and Ze
 e Grows A Tree are popular titles\, but we&#39\;d love to add more variety
 !
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center (Friends' Circle)\, 1405 
 S.R. 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260731T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260731T230000
UID:dd534ab0dcf5d291ee28e5dc5d9b7db4@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike around Lake Ogl
 e! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to excellen
 t views of the lake. Learn about July&#39\;s full moon\, the Buck Moon. Tr
 ail 7 is rated moderate\, but should be considered rugged in the dark. The
  trail has some staircases\, uneven surfaces\, and muddy spots. It is 1.2 
 miles and will take about an hour and a half to complete. Please do not br
 ing pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are preferred for night vision an
 d can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike cancellation policy : Hikes wil
 l be cancelled if there is lightning\, temperatures below 0 degrees Farenh
 eit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees Farenheit\, or a wind advisory
 . If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will be informed. The phone number f
 or the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Ogle parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\
 , Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T220000
UID:74a49be5b44deeb28c49433a02ebc323@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike around Lake Ogl
 e! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to excellen
 t views of the lake. Learn about August&#39\;s full moon\, the Sturgeon Mo
 on. Trail 7 is rated moderate\, but should be considered rugged in the dar
 k. The trail has some staircases\, uneven surfaces\, and muddy spots. It i
 s 1.2 miles and will take about an hour and a half to complete. Please do 
 not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are preferred for night vis
 ion and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike cancellation policy : Hik
 es will be cancelled if there is lightning\, temperatures below 0 degrees 
 Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees Farenheit\, or a wind ad
 visory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will be informed. The phone nu
 mber for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Ogle parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\
 , Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T203000
UID:d0b38f4b6d080ff34d5cdb28a2920016@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about September&#39\;s full moon t
 his year\, the Harvest Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but
  should be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slope
 s\, a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on w
 eather. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an hou
 r to complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights ar
 e preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike 
 cancellation policy : Hikes will be cancelled if there is lightning\, temp
 eratures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees
  Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will 
 be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
